---
// Act II — share. The collaboration story: a URL is the whole ceremony.
---

<section id="share" class="border-b border-[var(--border)] bg-[var(--bg-soft)]/50">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 py-20 max-sm:px-4 max-sm:py-14">
    <div
      class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_minmax(0,1.1fr)] lg:items-center lg:gap-14"
    >
      <div>
        <div
          class="font-mono text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-[var(--accent)]"
        >
          Share
        </div>
        <h2
          class="mt-3 font-sans text-[clamp(1.7rem,3.4vw,2.4rem)] font-bold leading-tight tracking-[-0.02em] text-[var(--bright)]"
        >
          Hand a teammate a URL.
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-[14.5px] leading-relaxed text-[var(--dim)]">
          <code class="text-[var(--code-fg)]">blit share</code> prints two links:
          one that types, one that watches. WebRTC punches through NATs — no SSH
          keys, no port forwarding, no account. The person on the other end gets
          the same workspace you saw above, in whatever browser they have.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-[14.5px] leading-relaxed text-[var(--dim)]">
          For machines you return to, name them once.
          <code class="text-[var(--code-fg)]">blit remote add prod ssh:alice@prod.co</code>
          — blit installs itself on the remote at first connection and every
          terminal there survives yours closing.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-5 border-t border-[var(--border)] pt-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed text-[var(--dim)]">
          Building your own front end? The same client ships as MIT-licensed
          packages — <code class="text-[var(--code-fg)]">@blit-sh/core</code> and
          Solid components — so a terminal in <em>your</em> product is an
          import, not a project.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div
        class="overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-[var(--border)] bg-[var(--code-bg)] shadow-lg"
        data-theme="dark"
      >
        <div
          class="border-b border-[var(--border)] bg-[var(--surface)] px-4 py-2 font-mono text-[10px] font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-[var(--dim)]"
        >
          Share & connect
        </div>
        <pre
          class="m-0 overflow-x-auto px-4 py-4 font-mono text-[13px] leading-relaxed text-[var(--code-fg)]"><code><span class="text-[var(--green)] select-none">$</span> blit share
Terminals at <span class="text-[var(--accent)] underline">https://blit.sh/s#psk=rf6e…</span>
Read-only:   <span class="text-[var(--accent)] underline">https://blit.sh/s#psk=EMPs…</span>

<span class="text-[var(--green)] select-none">$</span> blit remote add prod ssh:alice@prod.co
<span class="text-[var(--green)] select-none">$</span> blit --on prod terminal list
<span class="text-[var(--dim)]">2  build (running)</span>
<span class="text-[var(--dim)]">3  shell (idle)</span></code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
